   "priceMinor": 37400,
   "currency": "USD",
   "availability": "sold_out",
   "description": "Since 1937, The Bombay Hook National Wildlife Refuge has been a sanctuary for animals of all kinds, but most notably migratory birds which flock here by the hundreds of thousands every year. This 15,978-acre tidal salt marsh was known to the Native American as Canaresse –– meaning \"at the thickets” –– and later referred to as Ruyge-Bosje –– meaning “shaggy bushes.” Inspired, we designed our Bombay Hook watch so it could easily blend in without disturbing a single waterfowl. Note the forest-green display which contains a leafy silhouette, made complete by a suede band for a truly natural feel. Perfect for birdwatching incognito, or simply dressing to impress.",
