   "availability": "sold_out",
   "description": "Next to Cal Ripken, Baltimore’s most iconic figure is decidedly a bit more goth. Edgar Allen Poe lived in “Charm City” off and on throughout his life, which came to its mysterious conclusion there in 1849. But not before he wrote The Raven –– one of the spookiest, and most famous poems, ever published. To honor his singular work, our Raven timepiece is predominantly raven-black, with just a touch of blue on the bezel. Its gold-rimmed display features a graphic pattern reminiscent of overlapping feathers, perfect for brooding nights on the town… or perhaps sulking in one’s study “upon a midnight dreary.”",
